@startuml STM-10
!include _style.iuml
title STM-10 (System level) — Lifecycle of a Refund\nrefunds.status · v2.0 · 26/11/2026 · manual refund (decision D-AC)

[*] --> requested : Admin creates the refund request,\nor the system closes the account\n/ debit Charging Credit, return\nredeemed points, list for customer service
note left of requested
  kind top_up or late_payment: created by the Admin;
  kind account_closure: created by the system when
  a Driver closes the account. All wait in the same
  customer-service list (Billing Exceptions).
  Customer service refunds the amount in the
  VNPay merchant portal, outside PowerMe.
end note
requested --> done : Admin enters the gateway refund number\n[number not recorded before]\n/ request adjustment invoice (STM-7),\nnotify Driver (MSG25)
requested --> failed : Admin marks failed\n[gateway refused the refund]\n/ record reason
failed --> requested : Admin redoes the refund
done --> [*]
note right of failed
  The money stays with the refund request;
  it is never put back on the balance.
  No automatic sending, gateway query
  or retry for refunds.
end note
@enduml
